    "phi_of_symmetric_P_asymmetry_over_S4": 0.0,
    "commutes_with_permutations": true,
    "note": "Phi maps symmetric->symmetric BIT-EXACTLY (asymmetry of Phi(symmetric P) = 0.0, far below the 1e-12 target). The reduced phi_red = reduce(phi_full(expand(v))) is therefore exact; orbit-average vs representative-read agree to 4e-16."
  },
  "interpretation_gamma_0.1": {
    "genuine_fixed_point": "ONLY the fully-revealing point (FP0) is a true fixed point: ||F||inf = 9.45e-6 (NK floor ~1e-5), deficit = 1.1e-16, d_FR = 1.7e-10. P = lam(tau * sum_k u_k) essentially solves Phi(P)=P.",
    "naive_dedup_caveat": "The dedup counts 5 'distinct' low-residual points, but FP1-FP4 (||F||inf = 0.0088, 0.067, 0.067, 0.087) are NOT fixed points -- they are where Newton-Krylov STALLED on the non-smooth residual. Treating ||F||inf<0.005 as the genuine-FP bar, there is exactly ONE equilibrium (FR).",
    "(a)_unique_PR_equilibrium": "NO unique PR equilibrium. The unique genuine equilibrium at gamma=0.1 is FULLY-REVEALING (deficit ~0), NOT partially-revealing. This DIFFERS from K=3 (unique PR eq, deficit ~0.27). Adding a 4th identical agent appears to push the strict-h0 REE onto the FR manifold.",
    "(b)_nonsmooth_floor": "YES, recurs strongly. Every non-FR seed (NL, constant, both random) stalls at ||F||inf ~ 0.07-0.20; NK cannot drive below. Even the FR point has a residual FLOOR ~1e-5 (NK cannot reach machine zero) due to the non-differentiable contour-crossing decisions -- the same active-set non-smoothness that capped K=3 at ~0.2. The K=4 stall band (~0.07-0.2 for off-FR seeds) is comparable to K=3's ~0.2.",
    "(c)_picard_period2_oscillation": "NO. See picard_oscillation block: Picard from NL IC converges (deficit -> 0.0003, FR) with a small ~0.015 non-smooth ||F||inf plateau; no clean period-2 cycle. K=3's period-2 learning oscillation does NOT recur at K=4.",
    "summary_vs_K3": "Of the three K=3 structural features, K=4 reproduces the NON-SMOOTH RESIDUAL FLOOR (b) but NOT the unique-PR-equilibrium (a, K=4 is FR instead) and NOT the period-2 Picard oscillation (c, K=4 converges to FR)."
  },
